Remote Access Infrastructure
Overview
Remote access is delivered via a VPN-first architecture designed to securely connect authorized users to internal services without exposing administrative interfaces to the public internet. This strategy significantly reduces the attack surface while maintaining convenient access to infrastructure resources, hosted applications, and management tools.

The design supports administration, service management, media consumption, and application hosting, ensuring that sensitive management portals remain isolated from direct external access.

Design Objectives
Secure External Access: Enable safe connectivity to internal services from any location.
Minimize Exposure: Keep management interfaces private and accessible only via secure tunnels.
Encrypted Traffic: Ensure all data in transit is protected with modern encryption standards.
Streamlined Administration: Simplify the management of self-hosted infrastructure for remote operators.
Controlled Access: Grant permissions strictly to authorized users.
Consistent Experience: Provide a uniform user experience whether on-site or remote.
