Remote Access Strategy
Administrative services and core infrastructure components are kept private by default. Rather than exposing management portals directly to the internet, users establish a secure WireGuard VPN tunnel to access internal resources.

Protected Services Include:

Proxmox VE Management Interface
DNS Administration (Pi-hole/Unbound)
Infrastructure Monitoring Dashboards
Storage Management Interfaces
Authentication Platforms
Internal Development Applications
This approach drastically reduces the number of publicly exposed services, mitigating the risk of unauthorized access and brute-force attacks.

WireGuard Implementation
WireGuard was selected as the primary remote access solution due to its simplicity, high performance, and robust encryption standards.

Key Advantages:

Fast Handshake: Rapid connection establishment with minimal latency.
Efficiency: Low CPU and memory footprint compared to legacy solutions.
Modern Crypto: Built on state-of-the-art cryptographic primitives.
Cross-Platform: Native support across Linux, Windows, macOS, iOS, and Android.
Simplicity: Minimal configuration complexity compared to OpenVPN or IPsec.
Reliability: Stable connectivity even on fluctuating network conditions.
Public Service Access
While management tools remain behind the VPN, select user-facing applications are made accessible via the Traefik reverse proxy.

Examples:

media.example.com (Jellyfin)
cloud.example.com (Nextcloud)
services.example.com (Custom Apps)
These services are routed through Traefik with enforced HTTPS encryption and optional authentication controls, ensuring a secure public-facing layer.

